          "path": "_m/r/7/5/z/bunya-mountains-national-park-wk/statelibqld-2-393277-lucerne-p.jpg",
          "filename": "StateLibQld 2 393277 Lucerne Patch on National Reserve, Bunya Mountains, 1929.jpg",
          "caption": "Lucerne Patch on National Reserve, Bunya Mountains, 1929\nEuropean settlement spread rapidly across the Darling Downs and South Burnett during the 1840s and 1850s. It wasn't long before timber-getters were drawn to the abundant supply of red cedar and other valuable timber growing in the mountains. Cedar workers were tough and resourceful people, who felled trees and snigged them to sawpits to cut them up. Timber was carted to Dalby and other fledgling townships.",
          "alt": "Lucerne Patch on National Reserve, Bunya Mountains, 1929\nEuropean settlement spread rapidly across the Darling Downs and South Burnett during the 1840s and 1850s. It wasn't long before timber-getters were drawn to the abundant supply of red cedar and other valuable timber growing in the mountains. Cedar workers were tough and resourceful people, who felled trees and snigged them to sawpits to cut them up. Timber was carted to Dalby and other fledgling townships.",
          "width": 1000,
          "height": 729,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "Mears, E. H.",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:StateLibQld_2_393277_Lucerne_Patch_on_National_Reserve,_Bunya_Mountains,_1929.jpg",
